    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price (especially after sentiment > 0.00).",
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0.00) or near-zero, indicating bearish bias.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast is significantly above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "Increase downward bias when price history shows persistent downward trend (e.g., 3 consecutive days < 65.00).",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce next forecast by 5-10% to account for delayed reaction.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment spikes — use 3-day rolling average to smooth sentiment signals before adjusting forecasts."
  ]
